      "writtenOn": "2020-11-10T05:45:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to https://docs.python.org/3/library/csv.html#csv.DictReader this block doesn\u0027t ensure that all rows have been properly filled, assuming I understood your intentions here.\n\nTo be a bit more strict we could do something like this (includes the above comment too):\n\n1) This ensures that the row has the correct headers and no additional values (as those would have been mapped to the None key)\n\n  if tuple(row.keys()) !\u003d CSV_HEADERS:\n      # log_failure and return\n\n\n2) Ensure that there are no missing values. No need to set \u0027restval\u0027 to something else, given that AFAIK there is no way to have None as value from a CSV\n\n  if any(value is None for value in row.values()):\n      # log_failure and return\n\nThey could be combined in a single if, but separate we can give a more specific message to the user. Up to you.",
      "revId": "d2094ba7b56029c441ebb2eb922538a81b71304e",
      "serverId": "e9e9afe9-4712-486d-8885-f54b72dd1951",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a48ad57_5df9ffc8",
        "filename": "customscripts/interface_automation.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 835,
      "author": {
        "id": 4700
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-11T08:25:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is just to check that the headers are present, not the values.\n\nMy code is agnostic to the position of the headers (which I think is better) and tells which column is missing.",
      "parentUuid": "87471d20_7777c7fe",
      "revId": "d2094ba7b56029c441ebb2eb922538a81b71304e",
      "serverId": "e9e9afe9-4712-486d-8885-f54b72dd1951",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "748d1acf_19507f32",
        "filename": "customscripts/interface_automation.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 835,
      "author": {
        "id": 3215
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-16T15:24:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok to keep the order flexible. What I would suggest though is to add a check that all rows have the right amount of values. The CSV module uses:\n\n  If a row has more fields than fieldnames, the remaining data is put in a list and stored with \n  the fieldname specified by restkey (which defaults to None). If a non-blank row has fewer \n  fields than fieldnames, the missing values are filled-in with the value of restval (which \n  defaults to None).\n\nThat basically means checking if there is a None key in the row and if there is any value with None (point (2) from my previous comment).\n\nIt\u0027s not mandatory but IMHO we should fail and tell the user if the number of values differ from the number of columns in the CSV because it\u0027s a mistake and might lead to use wrong values for other fields that might still be \"valid\" and not make the script fail but allocate the device with wrong parameters.",
      "parentUuid": "8a48ad57_5df9ffc8",
      "revId": "d2094ba7b56029c441ebb2eb922538a81b71304e",
      "serverId": "e9e9afe9-4712-486d-8885-f54b72dd1951",
